1
00:00:00,383 --> 00:00:02,211
The universe could end right now,

2
00:00:02,514 --> 00:00:04,069
and you would never see it coming.

3
00:00:05,103 --> 00:00:07,463
Empty space is filled with the Higgs field.

4
00:00:07,716 --> 00:00:09,924
And it may be resting on a ledge, not

5
00:00:09,924 --> 00:00:10,939
the valley floor.

6
00:00:11,973 --> 00:00:14,348
If it ever slips through, at just one point,

7
00:00:14,601 --> 00:00:16,380
a bubble of new space is born.

8
00:00:17,413 --> 00:00:19,588
It grows at almost the speed of light.

9
00:00:19,841 --> 00:00:22,795
Inside, atoms as we know them cannot exist.

10
00:00:23,833 --> 00:00:24,698
No warning.

11
00:00:25,001 --> 00:00:27,591
The wall arrives right behind its own light.

12
00:00:28,623 --> 00:00:29,599
The good news?

13
00:00:29,903 --> 00:00:33,147
The best estimate for the wait is a 1

14
00:00:33,147 --> 00:00:35,075
followed by 139 zeros,

15
00:00:35,279 --> 00:00:36,038
in years.

16
00:00:37,073 --> 00:00:38,979
So, almost certainly not today.

17
00:00:39,487 --> 00:00:40,464
But if it did…
